Completed C109. The general neutral-sector bound remains unproved, but the missing inputs are explicit.

- Under dynamical CFT matching, locality gives \(v_a\le4eM\). Thus one minimal-model factor satisfies \(cv<4eM\), and one standard parafermion factor satisfies \(cv<8eM\). Uncontrolled multiplicity prevents a general sum bound.
- Discrete twists need a bound on \(L\,\Delta E_{\mathrm{twist}}\). The bond norm only bounds \(\Delta E_{\mathrm{twist}}\). Replica twists reduce exactly to C98 ring gluing.
- The spatial energy-current tail measures \(\sum c_av_a^4\). Moreover, a velocity floor is false already for a \(d=2\) Ising family with \(v=2\gamma\) and \(M=\sqrt{1+\gamma^2}\).
- A charged extension still needs a quantitative comparison of the original and extended Casimir coefficients.

